1
00:00:01,915 --> 00:00:05,755
Chapter 50. Ahab's boat and crew.

2
00:00:05,756 --> 00:00:08,159
Fidala.

3
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:12,638
Who would have thought at Flask? cried Stub. If I had but one leg, you would

4
00:00:12,639 --> 00:00:18,238
not catch me in a boat. Unless maybe to stop the plug hole with my timber toe.

5
00:00:18,239 --> 00:00:23,518
He is a wonderful old man. I don't think it's so strange after all on that

6
00:00:23,519 --> 00:00:28,318
account, said Flask. If his leg were off at the hip now, it would be a different

7
00:00:28,319 --> 00:00:32,719
thing. That would disable him. But he has one knee and a good part of the

8
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:35,198
other left, you know.

9
00:00:35,199 --> 00:00:41,039
I don't know that, my little man. I never yet saw him kneel.

10
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:45,274
Among whalewise people, it has often been argued whether, considering the

11
00:00:45,275 --> 00:00:49,594
paramount importance of his life to the success of the voyage, it is right for a

12
00:00:49,595 --> 00:00:54,878
whailing captain to jeopardize that life in the active perils of the chase. So

13
00:00:54,879 --> 00:00:59,198
Tamarlain soldiers often argued with tears in their eyes whether that

14
00:00:59,199 --> 00:01:04,079
invaluable life of his ought to be carried into the thickest of the fight.

15
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:08,799
But with Ahab the question assumed a modified aspect, considering that with

16
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:13,838
two legs man is but a hobbling white in all times of danger, considering that

17
00:01:13,839 --> 00:01:18,318
the pursuit of whales is always under great and extraordinary difficulties,

18
00:01:18,319 --> 00:01:23,435
that every individual moment indeed then comprises apparel. Under these

19
00:01:23,436 --> 00:01:29,274
circumstances, is it wise for any maimed man to enter a whaleboat in the hunt? As

20
00:01:29,275 --> 00:01:34,638
a general thing, the joint owners of the Peekquad must plainly have thought not.

21
00:01:34,639 --> 00:01:38,558
Ahab well knew that although his friends at home would think little of his

22
00:01:38,559 --> 00:01:43,755
entering a boat in certain comparatively harmless vicissitudes of the chase for

23
00:01:43,756 --> 00:01:48,318
the sake of being near the scene of action and giving his orders in person,

24
00:01:48,319 --> 00:01:52,638
yet for Captain Ahab to have a boat actually aortioned to him as a regular

25
00:01:52,639 --> 00:01:57,435
headsman in the hunt, above all for Captain Ahab to be supplied with five

26
00:01:57,436 --> 00:02:03,198
extra men as that same boat's crew. He well knew that such generous conceits

27
00:02:03,199 --> 00:02:08,079
never entered the heads of the owners of the Peekquad. Therefore, he had not

28
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:13,039
solicited a boat's crew from them, nor had he in any way hinted his desires on

29
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:18,079
that head. Nevertheless, he had taken private measures of his own touching all

30
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:22,558
that matter. Until Archie's published discovery, the sailors had little

31
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:27,435
foreseen it, though to be sure when, after being a little while out of port,

32
00:02:27,436 --> 00:02:31,518
all hands had concluded the customary business of fitting the whaleboats for

33
00:02:31,519 --> 00:02:36,558
service, when sometime after this Ahab was now and then found beering himself

34
00:02:36,559 --> 00:02:41,198
in the matter of making thole pins with his own hands for what was thought to be

35
00:02:41,199 --> 00:02:45,838
one of the spare boats, and even solicitously cutting the small wooden

36
00:02:45,839 --> 00:02:50,079
skewers, which when the line is running out, are pinned over the groove in the

37
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:55,039
bow. When all this was observed in him, and particularly his solicitude in

38
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:59,594
having an extra coat of sheathing in the bottom of the boat, as if to make it

39
00:02:59,595 --> 00:03:04,719
better withstand the pointed pressure of his ivory limb, and also the anxiety

40
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:09,999
heed in exactly shaping the thighboard, or clumsy cleat, as it is sometimes

41
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:14,238
called, the horizontal piece in the boat's bow for bracing the knee against,

42
00:03:14,239 --> 00:03:18,958
in darting or stabbing at the whale, when it was observed how often he stood

43
00:03:18,959 --> 00:03:23,838
up in that boat with his solitary knee fixed in the semic-ircular depression in

44
00:03:23,839 --> 00:03:28,238
the cleat, and with the carpenter's chisel, gouged out a little here, and

45
00:03:28,239 --> 00:03:32,399
straightened it a little there. All these things, I say, had awakened much

46
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:37,435
interest and curiosity at the time. But almost everybody supposed that this

47
00:03:37,436 --> 00:03:41,914
particular preparative heedfulness in Ahab must only be with a view to the

48
00:03:41,915 --> 00:03:46,399
ultimate chase of Moby Dick, for he had already revealed his intention to hunt

49
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:51,594
that mortal monster in person. But such a supposition did by no means involve

50
00:03:51,595 --> 00:03:57,679
the remotest suspicion as to any boat's crew being assigned to that boat.

51
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:02,719
Now with these subordinate phantoms, what wonder remained soon waned away,

52
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,755
for in a wher wonders soon Wayne.

53
00:04:05,756 --> 00:04:11,274
Besides, now and then such unaccountable odds and ends of strange nations come up

54
00:04:11,275 --> 00:04:15,914
from the unknown nooks and ash holes of the earth to man these floating outlaws

55
00:04:15,915 --> 00:04:20,558
of whalers, and the ships themselves often pick up such queer castaway

56
00:04:20,559 --> 00:04:25,914
creatures found tossing about the open sea on planks, bits of wreck, orars,

57
00:04:25,915 --> 00:04:32,238
whaleboats, canoes, blown off Japanese junks and whatnot, that Bezabub himself

58
00:04:32,239 --> 00:04:36,318
might climb up the side and step down into the cabin. to chat with the

59
00:04:36,319 --> 00:04:41,999
captain, and it would not create any unsubduable excitement in the folks.

60
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:46,318
But be all this as it may, certain it is, that while these subordinate

61
00:04:46,319 --> 00:04:50,638
phantoms soon found their place among the crew, though still, as it were,

62
00:04:50,639 --> 00:04:55,999
somehow distinct from them, yet that hair turbaned Fidala remained a muffled

63
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:01,679
mystery to the last. Once he came in a mannerly world like this, by what sort

64
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:06,159
of unaccountable tie he soon evinced himself to be linked with Ahab's

65
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:11,999
peculiar fortunes, nay, so far as to have some sort of half-hinted influence,

66
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:17,198
heaven knows, but it might have been even authority over him. All this none

67
00:05:17,199 --> 00:05:22,558
knew, but one cannot sustain an indifferent heir concerning Fidala. He

68
00:05:22,559 --> 00:05:26,958
was such a creature as civilized domestic people in the temperate zone

69
00:05:26,959 --> 00:05:32,719
only see in their dreams, and that but dimly, but the like of whom now and then

70
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:37,914
glide among the unchanging Asiatic communities, especially the oriental

71
00:05:37,915 --> 00:05:43,274
isles to the east of the continent, those insulated, immemorial, unalterable

72
00:05:43,275 --> 00:05:48,318
countries, which even in these modern days still preserve much of the ghostly

73
00:05:48,319 --> 00:05:52,958
aborigeness of the Earth's primal generations. when the memory of the

74
00:05:52,959 --> 00:05:58,238
first man was a distinct recollection, and all men his descendants, unknowing

75
00:05:58,239 --> 00:06:03,838
whence he came, eyed each other as real phantoms, and asked of the sun and the

76
00:06:03,839 --> 00:06:09,838
moon why they were created, and to what end, when, though, according to Genesis,

77
00:06:09,839 --> 00:06:14,878
the angels indeed consorted with the daughters of men, the devils also, add

78
00:06:14,879 --> 00:06:21,559
the unconical rabbines, indulged in mundane amors.
